# Cline rules — myAdmin (Kiro `.kiro` definitions → Cline / OpenRouter)

This workspace is governed by Kiro's `.kiro/` tree. Cline does not natively parse
Kiro's front-matter `inclusion:` modes, so the wiring below reproduces that load
behavior for Cline. Facts stay single-sourced in `.kiro/`; this file only points.

## Model provider

- AI calls go through **OpenRouter**: `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions`,
  key from env `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` (see `SETUP.md`, `README.md`).
- Model slug is chosen by Cline's model picker; OpenRouter features (invoice
  extraction, template assistant, budget AI) read the key from the backend env.

## Skills — load on demand by name

`.kiro/skills/<name>.md` carries operational how-to. Load the matching skill
before answering:

| Name | File | When |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `#commands` | `.kiro/skills/commands.md` | build/run/test commands, env setup |
| `#database` | `.kiro/skills/database.md` | DB connections, migrations, Railway ops |
| `#pr-checklist` | `.kiro/skills/pr-checklist.md` | reviewing a change |
| `#specs-reference` | `.kiro/skills/specs-reference.md` | spec structure/links |

## Steering — when a file must be in context

`.kiro/steering/` owns conventions; each file declares its mode:

- `auto` (always in context): `00`, `10`, `11`, `12`, `20`, `21`, `22`, `23`,
  `35`, `36`, `37`, `38`, `40`, `41`, `43`.
- `fileMatch` (only when editing matching files): `30` (backend routes/services),
  `31` (backend `*.py`), `32` (frontend `*.ts[x]`), `33` (frontend tests),
  `34` (`test_*.py`).
- `manual` (explicit request): `42` (local DynamoDB).

For `fileMatch`/`manual` work, read the matching `.kiro/steering/NN-*.md` first.

## Specs

Feature specs live in `.kiro/specs/<Area>/`. Check the area `README.md` index and
the `#specs-reference` skill before editing under a spec.
